<title>USA: CP&amp;L sees Harris 1 nuke back on line Fri.</title>
<headline>CP&amp;L sees Harris 1 nuke back on line Fri.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carolina Power and Light Co's 880 megawatt Harris 1 nuclear power unit, shut late Thursday for repairs, will likely be back on line today at 1530-1600 EST, the company said Friday.  </p>
<p>The unit, in New Hill, N.C., was shut 2300 EST Thursday to repair a steam leak in a turbine building, a company spokeswoman said, adding the repairs are almost complete.</p>
<p>((New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
</text>
